    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: New Riders Pre-Ride Inspection</h1>
    <p>A pre-ride inspection is the most useful thing a new rider can learn in ten minutes, and this page teaches it as a simple, repeatable ritual rather than a mechanic's mystery. The rental machine you meet at a Hanoi counter is a machine with a history you did not see, and the inspection is how you meet it honestly: a walk around its parts in order, a few gentle tests, and photographs of every mark that was there before you were. No prior knowledge is assumed, and nothing in the ritual requires strength, tools or courage, only ten unhurried minutes and a phone.</p>
    <p>The page sits in the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster and is written for new riders. The verified price ladder lives on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, the general question bank is on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, and the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/how-to-rent-a-motorbike-in-hanoi/">how-to-rent guide</a> walks the whole counter sequence this inspection belongs to.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">Why the first ten minutes matter most</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">The walk-around, step by step</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">Tyres and brakes, the two big checks</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">Lights, horn and mirrors</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">Photographing the marks, the beginner's armor</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-6">Asking for a different bike</a></li>
